Plain Text\nexport endnote Endnote (file)\nexport refworks Refworks\n\nRequest / recall this title\n(2-3 business days)\n[Cover--Click to expand.]\n[Add this title to your marked items list]\nAdd\nThe meadow\nBarbara Bosworth, Margot Anne Kelley.\nAuthor: \tBosworth, Barbara, 1953- photographer, author.\nPublished: \tSanta Fe : Radius Books, [2015]\nCopyright: \t©2015\nDescription: \t199 pages, 53 unnumbered pages : color illustrations, facsimiles, maps ; 33 cm + 1 map (42 x 30 cm, folded to 23 x 30 cm) + 1 booklet (40 pages ; 29 cm)\nFormat: \tBook\nSummary:\nEmily Dickinson wrote that all it takes to make a prairie is \"one clover, and a bee. / And revery.\" It turns out that to know a prairie (or meadow ) is a bit more complicated, as photographer Barbara B osworth and writer Margot Anne Kelley have discovered. For more than a decade, Bosworth and Kelley have meandered in, studied and photographed a single meadow in Carlisle, Massachusetts. In addition to their own investigations, they have invited botanists, entomologists, naturalists and historians to consider the meadow with them. Also included are historic maps of the property dating to the 1800s, and a transcription of notes from a former owner whose family has continuously documented plant and bird life in the meadow from 1931 until the 1960s.\nPart photo-essay, part journal and part scientific study, this book is a meditation on the shifting perspective that occurs when one repeatedly sees the same place through new eyes.\nContent provided by Syndetic Solutions, Inc. Terms of Use\n... ( see more )\n\n    Subjects\n    Location\n    Table of Contents\n    MARC\n    Full Record\n\nSubjects\nMeadows -- Massachusetts -- Carlisle -- Pictorial works.\nPhotography, Artistic.\nCarlisle (Mass.) -- Pictorial works.\n\nOther Author: \t+Margot+Anne%2C\"&follow=Author\">Kelley, Margot Anne , author.\nLocation\nOnline\nLocation \tCall # \tStatus \tNotes\nArt Library \tTR655 .B67 2015 \tAvailable \t\nArt Library \tTR655 